<title>VENEZUELA: FOCUS-Oil price rise sees Venezuela newly prudent?.</title>
<headline>FOCUS-Oil price rise sees Venezuela newly prudent?.</headline>
<byline>John Paul Rathbone</byline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>In Venezuela the recent rise in international oil prices to five-year highs recalls the humble lottery winner's oft-heard line: this won't change my life.</p>
<p>But with a twist. For as Venezuela looks to reap at least $2.5 billion windfall from surging oil prices, the long held hope is precisely that Venezuela will change its ways and drop its spendthrift habits of the past 30 years.</p>
</text>
